Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:04:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DSV4: DSV4_WO_A_FP8_STORE keeps wo_a as fp8 + block scales
 (exact)

VllmDeepseekV4WoALinearMethod stores wo_a as an exact bf16 copy
(64 MiB/layer, 2.7 GiB/chip replicated under attention DP). With
DSV4_WO_A_FP8_STORE=1 (default off) the processed fp8 weight and its
power-of-two block scales are kept instead, and _o_proj rebuilds the bf16
weight per call with the same dequantize_linear_weight (moved to
layers/common/quantization/linear_dequant.py) and a unit scale, so the
kernel sees identical inputs. Saves ~1.3 GiB/chip for one layer's bf16
wo_a transient per call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MQhK9cavqLsEnxm6YHREB3
